  ],
  "notes": "Composed of {奮|ふん} (to stir up, exert) + {起|き} (to rise). Describes the act of summoning courage or energy, especially after adversity. Often used in sports, business, and motivational contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {奮起|ふんき}を{促|うなが}す: to urge someone to rally\n- {奮起|ふんき}して{立|た}ち{上|あ}がる: to rouse oneself and stand up\n- {一念発起|いちねんほっき}: to resolve to do something (similar idiom)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {奮闘|ふんとう}する: to struggle hard — emphasizes the effort and fighting spirit during a task\n- {発奮|はっぷん}する: to be inspired — focuses on the spark of motivation\n- {頑張|がんば}る: to do one's best — more casual and general-purpose",
